% Sync: The Drawbridge (one crosses and lowers the bridge; mist, then throw)
%
% A sentinel machine stands on a ledge beyond a gulf. It is heavy: nothing
% moves it. The drawbridge over the gulf is raised, and its winch is on the
% far pier. Three companions: the player and the mage pick one skill each
% from seven; the porter only knows turnToMist. Nobody can do the job from
% the dock - the ledge is out of sight - so one companion crosses on its
% own and lowers the bridge, and the others walk over and finish it.
%
%   dock (player, mage, porter) ~~ gulf ~~ pier [winch] --- ledge (sentinel) ~~ cliff
%      \                                /      |
%       ------- drawbridge (door) -----       stair --- overlook (across the cliff)
%
% The moment: the porter turns the sentinel to mist - for a moment it is not
% heavy. The moment lasts through the next cast by anyone, so the very next
% cast must be the one that throws it: mist, then throw, back to back.
%
% Obstacles and every method:
%   the gulf       nobody walks over it, and the bridge is up. Blink onto
%                  the pier, or lightningFlash there (a dash). Arriving on
%                  the pier works the winch: the drawbridge comes down for
%                  good, and the others walk over.
%   the sentinel   drop it off the ledge into the cliff, right after the
%                  porter's mist: fireball or tidalWave it from the pier (a
%                  push), hook or taunt it from the overlook (dragged across
%                  the cliff, it falls in), or vortex the cliff (everything
%                  next to it is sucked in). Or short it, with no mist at
%                  all: tidalWave soaks it, lightningFlash jolts it.
%
% Traps:
%   - no line of sight from the dock to the ledge: nothing is done from the
%     near side;
%   - the crossing skills move only their caster, and none of them throws
%     the sentinel;
%   - heavy, the sentinel does not budge: a push without the mist just
%     before it does nothing, and so does a cast in between;
%   - a dry jolt only stuns a machine (it is not out of the fight).
%
% Hypothesis (design.md): no single skill wins; 20 of 49 assignments win
% (each crossing skill with each thrower, either seat), by 11 methods.

% === Regions ===
region(dock).
region(gulf).
region(pier).
region(drawbridge).
region(ledge).
region(cliff).
region(stair).
region(overlook).
connected(dock, gulf).
connected(gulf, dock).
connected(gulf, pier).
connected(pier, gulf).
connected(dock, drawbridge).
connected(drawbridge, dock).
connected(drawbridge, pier).
connected(pier, drawbridge).
connected(pier, ledge).
connected(ledge, pier).
connected(ledge, cliff).
connected(cliff, ledge).
connected(pier, stair).
connected(stair, pier).
connected(stair, overlook).
connected(overlook, stair).

lineOfSight(dock, pier).
lineOfSight(pier, dock).
lineOfSight(pier, ledge).
lineOfSight(pier, cliff).
lineOfSight(overlook, ledge).
lineOfSight(overlook, cliff).

% The route over the gulf, for leaps: only forward.
progress(dock, 0).
progress(gulf, 1).
progress(drawbridge, 1).
progress(pier, 2).
progress(ledge, 3).
progress(stair, 3).
progress(overlook, 4).

% A push from the pier on the ledge lands in the cliff; from the overlook,
% the cliff lies between it and the ledge.
beyond(pier, ledge, cliff).
beyond(overlook, cliff, ledge).

% === Terrain ===
onEnter(gulf, chasm).
onEnter(cliff, chasm).
door(drawbridge).
onEnter(pier, winch).
effect(winch, target, open(drawbridge)).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
role(porter, companion).
at(player, dock).
at(mage, dock).
at(porter, dock).
mana(player, 4).
mana(mage, 4).
knows(porter, turnToMist).

% === The sentinel ===
role(sentinel, enemy).
at(sentinel, ledge).
tag(sentinel, machine).
tag(sentinel, heavy).

% === Default kit: one skill each (combos replans the whole matrix) ===
knows(player, blink).
knows(mage, fireball).

% === Victory ===
% Someone gets onto the pier (the bridge comes down), then the sentinel goes.
win :- if(), do(lowerBridge, neutralize(sentinel)).

lowerBridge :- if(canAct(?a)), do(reach(?a, pier), opened(drawbridge)).
opened(?d) :- if(open(?d)), do().

funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).

% === Choice: one skill each, from seven (htn_components combos) ===
% The porter keeps turnToMist.
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(blink).
comboPool(lightningFlash).
comboPool(fireball).
comboPool(tidalWave).
comboPool(hook).
comboPool(taunt).
comboPool(vortex).
comboMinWins(8).
comboMinMethods(4).

goals(win).
